{"seconds": 47.0, "exit": 0, "final": "Only one legal move: Kxg7. The king on h8 cannot move anywhere else because f8 is blocked by the rook. So after Nf6+ Kh8 Qxg7+ Kxg7 (forced), White continues the attack.\n\nThe best move is **Nf6+**, and the main forcing line shows this is winning.\n\n---\n\n**Coaching Note (80 words max):**\n\nWhen the opponent has a pinned piece\u2014especially a pawn next to the king\u2014look for forcing moves that exploit that weakness. Here, Black's g7 pawn is pinned to the king on g8 by your queen. The knight check on f6 is devastating: if the king moves to h8, Qxg7# is checkmate (the king has no escape). If Black captures with Qxf6, you continue Qxg7+ and win material. This is a classic pattern: **pin + forcing check = decisive advantage.**\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nf6+\", \"line\": [\"Nf6+\", \"Kh8\", \"Qxg7+\", \"Kxg7\", \"Nh5+\", \"Kg6\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"pin\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/5pp1/3p4/p2Nq3/1p2P1Q1/1P6/1P3RKP/4r3 w - - 1 32"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/5pp1/3p4/p2Nq3/1p2P1Q1/1P6/1P3RKP/4r3 w - - 1 32"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/5pp1/3p4/p2Nq3/1p2P1Q1/1P6/1P3RKP/4r3 w - - 1 32"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/5pp1/3p4/p2Nq3/1p2P1Q1/1P6/1P3RKP/4r3 w - - 1 32", "move": "Nf6+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/5pp1/3p4/p2Nq3/1p2P1Q1/1P6/1P3RKP/4r3 w - - 1 32", "move": "Ne7+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/5pp1/3p4/p2Nq3/1p2P1Q1/1P6/1P3RKP/4r3 w - - 1 32", "move": "Qxg7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/5pp1/3p1N2/p3q3/1p2P1Q1/1P6/1P3RKP/4r3 b - - 2 32", "move": "Qxf6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/5pp1/3p1N2/p3q3/1p2P1Q1/1P6/1P3RKP/4r3 b - - 2 32", "move": "Kh8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen":